# Layout Components

## Component Structure

```
src/components/features/
├── layout/
│   ├── nav-bar.tsx            # Compact search, nav items, country selector
│   ├── footer.tsx
│   ├── theme-toggle.tsx       # Standalone toggle (used in mobile menu only)
│   ├── country-selector.tsx   # Country selection for watch providers
│   ├── mobile-bottom-nav.tsx  # Native-app-style bottom navigation
│   └── scroll-to-top.tsx      # Scroll restoration on route changes
├── hover-card/                 # Netflix-style hover card system
│   ├── index.ts               # Export hub
│   ├── hover-card-context.tsx # Global state (only one hover card open at a time)
│   ├── hover-card-overlay.tsx # Positioned overlay with edge detection
│   └── hover-card-wrapper.tsx # Wrapper for any card component
├── search/
│   ├── index.ts
│   └── search-command.tsx     # Dialog with Command for global search
├── auth/
│   ├── index.ts               # Export hub for auth components
│   ├── google-one-tap.tsx     # Google One Tap prompt (non-invasive)
│   ├── login-dialog.tsx       # Manual sign-in modal
│   ├── user-menu.tsx          # Avatar dropdown (profile, watchlist, appearance, logout)
│   └── settings-menu.tsx      # Settings dropdown for non-auth users (card display, theme)
└── providers/
    ├── index.tsx              # Main providers wrapper (auth, theme, query, etc.)
    └── user-store-provider.tsx # Hydrates user store on auth changes
```

## NavBar Patterns

The navbar uses scroll-aware styling with compact, left-aligned elements. **Hidden on mobile** - `MobileBottomNav` handles navigation instead.

**Desktop NavBar:**
- Hidden on mobile: `hidden md:block`
- Scroll-aware background (transparent → solid on scroll)
- Compact search button with keyboard shortcut (⌘K / Ctrl+K)

**Search Button (Compact):**
```tsx
// Small button with search icon + keyboard shortcut (not a wide search bar)
<button onClick={() => setSearchOpen(true)} className="...">
  <Search className="h-4 w-4" />
  <kbd className="hidden lg:inline-flex h-5 ...">
    {isMac ? "⌘" : "Ctrl"}K
  </kbd>
</button>
```

**Scroll-Aware Styling:**
```tsx
// Nav items adapt to scroll state (transparent vs solid background)
<Button
  variant="ghost"
  className={cn(
    "gap-2",
    isScrolled
      ? "text-foreground/80 hover:text-foreground hover:bg-accent"
      : "text-white/90 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/10",
    pathname?.startsWith(href) && (isScrolled ? "bg-accent" : "bg-white/10")
  )}
>
```

**Right-Side Elements:**
- Compact search button (icon + shortcut)
- Country selector
- **Auth users**: UserMenu (includes card display + theme toggle in Appearance submenu)
- **Non-auth users**: SettingsMenu (cog icon) + Sign In button

**Settings Toggle Locations:**
- **Card Display**: Top of Appearance submenu (Poster Cards / Wide Cards)
- **Theme Mode**: Below card display (Light / Dark / System)
- **Color Theme**: Below mode (Default / Midnight Blue / Forest Green)

| Setting | Auth Users | Non-Auth Users |
|---------|------------|----------------|
| Card Display | UserMenu → Appearance | SettingsMenu |
| Theme Mode | UserMenu → Appearance | SettingsMenu |
| Color Theme | UserMenu → Appearance | SettingsMenu |

## MobileBottomNav Component

Native-app-style bottom navigation bar for mobile devices. Shows on screens < md (768px).

```
src/components/features/layout/mobile-bottom-nav.tsx
```

**Layout:**
```
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Home    Browse    Search    Watchlist    You/Menu            │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
         │                                      │
         └──────────────────────────────────────┘
                    h-14, fixed bottom-0
```

**Nav Items:**
| Position | Item | Icon | Behavior |
|------|----|------|---------|
| 1 | Home | `Home` | Links to `/` |
| 2 | Browse | `Compass` | Links to `/browse` |
| 3 | Search | `Search` | Opens SearchCommand dialog |
| 4 | Watchlist | `Bookmark` | Links to `/watchlist` |
| 5 | You/Menu | `User` or Avatar | Opens MobileUserSheet |

**User Avatar Display:**
- **Authenticated**: Shows user's avatar image or initials fallback
- **Unauthenticated**: Shows generic User icon with "Menu" label

```tsx
// User avatar with initials fallback (matches desktop navbar pattern)
{isAuthenticated ? (
  <Avatar className="h-5 w-5 ring-1 ring-border/40">
    {user?.image && <AvatarImage src={user.image} ... />}
    <AvatarFallback>{getInitials(user?.name || "U")}</AvatarFallback>
  </Avatar>
) : (
  <User className="h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground/70" />
)}
```

**Mobile User Sheet:**
- Bottom sheet (slides up from bottom)
- Shows user profile when authenticated
- Links: Watchlist, Watched, My Ratings, Settings
- Theme toggle with visual switch
- Sign In / Sign Out action

**Key implementation details:**
- Nav height: `h-14` (56px)
- Background: `bg-background/95 backdrop-blur-xl border-t border-border/30`
- Search uses `useSearchCommand` hook to control SearchCommand dialog
- AssistantFloaty (AI bubble) floats above the nav at `bottom-[4.25rem]`

**Usage in layout.tsx:**
```tsx
<Providers>
  <ScrollToTop />
  <NavBar />
  <main className="flex-1 pb-16 md:pb-0">{children}</main>  {/* pb-16 for mobile nav */}
  <Footer className="hidden md:block" />
  <MobileBottomNav />
</Providers>
```

## CountrySelector Component

Dropdown for selecting watch provider region:

```tsx
import { CountrySelector } from "@/components/features/layout";

// In NavBar
<CountrySelector />

// Compact mode (flag only)
<CountrySelector compact />
```

**Features:**
- Uses `country-list` library for complete country list (250+ countries)
- Priority countries (IN, US, UK, CA, AU, DE, FR, JP) shown at top
- Searchable with flag icons from `flagcdn.com`
- Stores selection in `countryOverride` (Zustand user store)
- Client-side only (not persisted to server)

**Design specs:**
- Button: Flag icon + country code (e.g., 🇮🇳 IN)
- Popover: 260px wide, 300px scroll area
- Search input at top for filtering

## HoverCard System (Netflix-style)

Enhanced hover card that provides quick preview of movie/series info when hovering over cards. Shows ratings, genres, cast, and watch options in a sleek overlay.

```
src/components/features/hover-card/
├── index.ts                  # Export hub
├── hover-card-context.tsx    # Global state management (ensures only one card open)
├── hover-card-overlay.tsx    # Main overlay component with positioning logic
└── hover-card-wrapper.tsx    # Wrapper component for any card
```

### Usage

The `HoverCardWrapper` wraps any card component to enable hover functionality:

```tsx
import { HoverCardWrapper } from "@/components/features/hover-card";

// Wrap individual cards
<HoverCardWrapper item={movie}>
  <MovieCard item={movie} />
</HoverCardWrapper>

// Already integrated in MediaCard
<MediaCard item={movie} enableHover />  // Default: enabled on desktop
```

### Provider Setup

`HoverCardProvider` is already included in the main providers wrapper:

```tsx
// src/components/providers/index.tsx
<HoverCardProvider>
  {children}
  <HoverCardOverlay />  {/* Portal to body */}
</HoverCardProvider>
```

### Server Action

Lean API endpoint (`src/server/actions/hover-card.ts`) returns only essential data:

```typescript
interface HoverCardData {
  id: number;
  title: string;
  backdrop_path: string | null;
  poster_path: string | null;
  year: string | null;
  runtime?: number;           // Movies only
  number_of_seasons?: number; // Series only
  genres: { id: number; name: string }[];
  ratings: { name: string; rating: string; certified?: boolean; sentiment?: string }[];
  cast: { id: number; name: string; character?: string; profile_path: string | null }[];
  watch_options: ProcessedWatchOptions;
}

// Usage in components
import { getHoverCardData } from "@/server/actions/hover-card";

const data = await getHoverCardData(movieId, "movie");
```

**Payload size:** ~2-3KB vs ~50KB+ for full movie details

### Design Specs

- **Width:** 440px
- **Edge detection:** Automatically positions to stay within viewport
- **Hover delay:** 500ms default (configurable via `delay` prop)
- **Animation:** Scale + fade with spring easing

### Hover Card Content Layout

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  [Backdrop Image - 16:9 aspect ratio]               │
