### Search Action

The `quickSearch` server action (`src/server/actions/search.ts`):

```typescript
// Returns unified results in TMDB relevance order
export async function quickSearch(query: string): Promise<QuickSearchResponse> {
  if (!query.trim()) return { results: [] };

  const response = await search({ query, page: 1 });
  return { results: response.results.slice(0, 8) };
}

// Full search (for /search page)
export async function search(input): Promise<SearchResponse> {
  // Returns results, movies, series, people (categorized for full page)
}
```

### Keyboard Shortcuts

The `useSearchCommand` hook manages Cmd+K (Mac) / Ctrl+K (Windows):

```tsx
export function useSearchCommand() {
  const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(false);

  React.useEffect(() => {
    const down = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
      if (e.key === "k" && (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey)) {
        e.preventDefault();
        setOpen((prev) => !prev);
      }
    };
    document.addEventListener("keydown", down);
    return () => document.removeEventListener("keydown", down);
  }, []);

  return { open, setOpen };
}
```

## User Library Pages Pattern

The user library pages (watchlist, ratings, watched) share a common pattern:

```
src/app/watchlist/     # Movies + Series user wants to watch
├── page.tsx           # Server component with metadata
└── client.tsx         # Tabbed Movies/Series view

src/app/ratings/       # Movies + Series user has liked/disliked
├── page.tsx           # Server component with metadata
└── client.tsx         # Filtered grid with type + rating toggles

src/app/watched/       # Movies user has marked as watched
├── page.tsx           # Server component with metadata
└── client.tsx         # Searchable grid with genre filter
```

### Common Patterns

All user library pages:
- Use TanStack Query for client-side data fetching
- Show unauthenticated state with sign-in prompt
- Pass `hideUserStatus` to cards (status is redundant on these pages)
- Support search, filter, and sort controls

### Data Fetching

Use TanStack Query for client-side data fetching with optimistic hydration:

```tsx
const { data: watchlist, isLoading } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ["watchlist"],
  queryFn: () => fetch("/api/user/watchlist").then(r => r.json()),
  enabled: authStatus === "authenticated",
  staleTime: 30000,
});
```
